items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md-85-1.2 Assume condition 1 FAILS. Negating the quantifiers of [L1], there is a real $\varepsilon_0 > 0$ such that for every real $\delta > 0$ some $x \in A$ has $0 < |x - c| < \delta$ and $|f(x) - L| \ge \varepsilon_0$. [assume-hyp, L1, L6]
