items/ex-rational-function-field-order.md-89-- **Why the eventual sign, and not the sign at a point.** Evaluating at a fixed
items/ex-rational-function-field-order.md-90-  real $x_0$ is not even a function on $\mathbb{R}(t)$, since a rational
items/ex-rational-function-field-order.md-91-  function may have a pole at $x_0$; and the sign at a point would not give a
items/ex-rational-function-field-order.md-92-  positive cone, because $t$ and $t - 1$ would then be incomparable in the wrong
items/ex-rational-function-field-order.md:93:  way. The behaviour at $+\infty$ is the unique choice that is representative
items/ex-rational-function-field-order.md-94-  independent and multiplicative, and step 1.1 is exactly that statement.
